//! # DAEMONIORUM
//!
//! A psychological horror game built on Sigil's native plurality system.
//! This game explores DID/plurality mechanics through horror gameplay,
//! where different alters perceive reality differently and must work
//! together to survive.
//!
//! ## Core Systems
//!
//! - **Plurality System**: Manage a system of alters with distinct
//!   personalities, abilities, and perceptions.
//!
//! - **Reality Layers**: See the world through three perception modes:
//!   Grounded (normal), Fractured (something's wrong), Shattered (full horror).
//!
//! - **Combat**: Turn-based combat where different alters have different
//!   combat roles and abilities.
//!
//! - **Dialogue**: Alter-aware dialogue trees where responses change based
//!   on who is fronting.
//!
//! - **Scenes**: Locations with reality layer variations and alter-specific
//!   observations.
//!
//! - **Events**: Trigger system connecting emotional stimuli to alter responses.
//!
//! ## Sigil Features Used
//!
//! - **Evidentiality Types**: `!` (known), `~` (reported), `?` (uncertain), `‽` (paradox)
//! - **Morpheme Operators**: `|τ` (transform), `|φ` (filter), `|∀` (forAll), `|∃` (exists)
//! - **Incorporation Syntax**: `·` for method chains
//! - **Actor System**: Message-passing concurrency for game loop
//! - **Native Plurality**: `alter`, `switch`, `cocon` declarations

